---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { APPLE_SUBSCRIPTIONS_URL, SUPPORT_EMAIL, SUPPORT_MAILTO } from '../config/site';
import '../styles/prose.css';

// Steps mirror apps/mobile/src/screens/PrivacyDataScreen.tsx and SettingsScreen.tsx.
// Re-check labels against the final release build before launch.
---

<Base
  title="Delete your account or data"
  description="How to delete your Okyo account or the Okyo data stored on your device."
>
  <div class="container page">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Delete your Okyo account or data</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">
        You can delete the Okyo data stored on your device, and delete a signed-in account, from
        inside the app.
      </p>

      <section class="panel">
        <h2>Delete your account (signed in with Apple or Google)</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Okyo and go to the <strong>Settings</strong> tab.</li>
          <li>Under <strong>Privacy &amp; account</strong>, open <strong>Privacy &amp; data</strong>.</li>
          <li>Tap <strong>Delete account</strong>, then <strong>Continue</strong>.</li>
          <li>Confirm again by tapping <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>If your session has expired, Okyo asks you to sign in again first.</p>
        <p>
          This permanently deletes your Okyo account, any linked purchase-management record, and the
          data saved on this device. It cannot be undone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel">
        <h2>Delete your data (no account needed)</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Okyo and go to the <strong>Settings</strong> tab.</li>
          <li>Open <strong>Privacy &amp; data</strong>.</li>
          <li>Tap <strong>Delete all my data</strong> and confirm.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          This removes locally stored recipes, scan and cooking history, grocery state, preferences,
          progress, and stored scan images. It cannot be undone. Uninstalling Okyo also removes the
          data stored by the app on that device.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What deletion does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            It does not cancel an App Store subscription. Cancel it with Apple:{' '}
            <a href={APPLE_SUBSCRIPTIONS_URL}>manage subscriptions</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Delete all my data</strong> only removes data on this device. It does not delete
            an account.
          </li>
          <li>
            It cannot remove purchase records that Apple or RevenueCat keep, or copies an AI service
            provider keeps, under their own retention rules.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Can't open the app?</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href={SUPPORT_MAILTO}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> and ask for your Okyo account to be
          deleted. Say whether you signed in with Apple or Google.
        </p>
        <div class="pending" data-pending="legal-review">
          <p><strong>Pending legal review:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>How Okyo will verify your identity before deleting an account by email.</li>
            <li>How quickly Okyo will respond to and complete an email deletion request.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
